{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794234544,"nonce":"iMZzwqjxhAo9D/Zt/YBvp2ZvUBA=","title":"jno.np.vector of bound components drops the coordinate binding","message":"vec(Et[0], Et[1], 0.0 * Et[2]) with Et = u.bind(x=xt, y=yt, z=zt) returns a VectorView with no coordinate Variables (_spatial_coord_vars is empty), so the region it was bound to is lost. Each component Et[i] still carries the coordinates. A term that relies only on such a vector for its region cannot be classified; the face operator falls back to the region of the term it is integrated in.","files":null}]}